  "notes": "USAGE:\nThe transitive counterpart of {揺|ゆ}るぐ (to shake, to be shaken — intransitive). Sense 2 (figurative undermining) is more common than sense 1 in news and written contexts. Often used with {基盤|きばん} (foundations), {信頼|しんらい} (trust), or {体制|たいせい} (system) as the object.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {信頼|しんらい}を{揺|ゆ}るがす: to shake trust\n- {基盤|きばん}を{揺|ゆ}るがす: to undermine the foundations\n- {世界|せかい}を{揺|ゆ}るがす: to shake the world\n- {根底|こんてい}から{揺|ゆ}るがす: to shake from the very bottom\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {揺|ゆ}るぐ: to shake, to waver (intransitive)\n- {揺|ゆ}らす: to shake, to swing (transitive, more gentle motion)\n- {揺|ゆ}れる: to sway, to shake (intransitive, general)",
